# Publish APK on every app change

Whenever you commit or push changes that affect the Android app (anything under `android/`, or release/version metadata the APK depends on):

1. Finish the git commit/push first (use the commit-and-push skill when the user asked to commit/push).
2. Immediately run:

```powershell
python scripts/publish_release.py
```

3. Confirm output includes `STATUS=ok` and the APK URL.

Do this automatically — do not wait for the user to ask to republish. Skip only for pure docs-only commits that do not change the built APK.

The script rebuilds the signed release APK and replaces the asset on the latest GitHub Release (`v1.0.0` by default).
